- file: scratchpad/effected/yaml/internal/composer/block.ts:1252
- class: bug   severity: required
- standard: D9, D11; PORT_LEDGER composer-cr-lines (`labBehaviour`: composer same-line checks recognize lone CR). evidence: `sameLine` / `lineIndentColumn` in `internal/composer/state.ts` stop on `\r` and `\n`. `sameLineSpan` (`comments.ts:139-141`) returns false only for `\n`. `columnAt` (`comments.ts:467`) and `blankLineAboveStart` (`comments.ts:274`) and `trimDisownedTrailingComments` (`block.ts:231`, `block.ts:238`) locate line starts with `lastIndexOf("\n")`. `composer-regressions.test.ts:224-234` pins `getLineStarts`, `lineCol`, `lineIndentColumn`, `sameLine`, and scalar continuations only.
- failure: Lone CR stays one line for comment ownership and one document-absolute column for terminal-comment partition, while structure and `seqIndent` already use real columns. For `a: # kc\r  1`, `trailingOnKey` at `block.ts:1252` is false, so the comment is stored on the value and stringifies as `a: 1 # kc`; the LF document stores it on the key and stringifies as `a: # kc` / `  1`. The same predicate at `block.ts:1365` and `block.ts:1422` stores `# lead` in `a:\r# lead\r  1` as a same-line trailing comment. `columnAt(...) < contentColumn` (`block.ts:1295`) and `columnAt(...) < seqIndent` (`block.ts:2329`) keep a column-0 `# tail` on the inner block. `hasBlankLineAbove` misses the blank in `a: 1\r\r# next`, and a comment that is escaped is not cut out of the node span.
- fix: Use the same lone-CR and single-CRLF breaks as `sameLine` and `lineIndentColumn` in `sameLineSpan`, `columnAt`, `blankLineAboveStart`, and both `lastIndexOf("\n")` scans in `trimDisownedTrailingComments`. Add a lone-CR pair-comment and nested `# tail` regression next to the existing CR line-index test.

